# Build System and Development Setup

This project uses Vite as its build tool and development server. The setup has been migrated from Grunt and Bower to modern tooling.

## Development

To start the development server:
```bash
npm run dev
```

This will start the Vite development server with hot module replacement enabled.

## Dependencies

The project uses npm for dependency management. Key dependencies include:
- Vite - Build tool and development server
- @svgdotjs/svg.js - SVG manipulation
- eventbusjs - Event handling
- modernizr - Feature detection
- classie - Class utilities

## Project Structure

- [app/](mdc:app) - Main application directory
  - [index.html](mdc:app/index.html) - Main entry point
  - [scripts/](mdc:app/scripts) - JavaScript source files
  - [styles/](mdc:app/styles) - CSS styles
  - [images/](mdc:app/images) - Image assets

## Build Configuration

The project uses ES modules and modern JavaScript features. The Vite configuration is set up to:
- Handle SVG files
- Process CSS
- Support ES modules
- Enable hot module replacement

## Migration Notes

The project has been migrated from:
- Grunt → Vite
- Bower → npm
- CommonJS → ES Modules

All SVG animations and interactions have been preserved during the migration.
